Paper summary
-------------
The paper proposes a hardware/software co-design to reduce the size of the memory dependence predictor (MDP) while maintaining performance. The key idea is to utilize profiling (with training inputs) to detect loads that can safely skip querying the MDP (independent with older yet to be executed stores); this information is encoded into a newly introduced ISA instruction so that the hardware can skip the query and also entry creation upon memory order violation.

Strengths
---------
- Simple design
- Paper is easy to follow

Weaknesses
----------
- Performance improvement is marginal relative to the cost
- Profiling pipeline is underspecified
- Workload coverage is too narrow

How easy is the paper easy to read and understand?
